{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CedMy9KVCaXQCiCSCMSdQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"WI-554 is complete and closed. Here's the summary.\n\n## What was wrong (OI-71, from round 019 of the wi508 lane)\n\nTwo defects in the re-attestation brief renderer (`trace.py --approve modified`), both on trunk and reproducible on any lane that regenerates the brief:\n\n1. **A `Drafted` row shown as approved.** `_cell_diff_lines` split a changed row's cells into the §A5.1 groups `approved — re-attestation owed` / `traced — routes to adjudication` keyed on the cell's *column class* alone, independent of the row's Status. A `Drafted` row that drifted in both an approved-class cell (a TC `Method`) and a traced-class cell (`Evidence`) rendered its `Method` change under **\"approved — re-attestation owed\"** — asserting a re-attestation window on a row that was never approved.\n\n2. **A changed cell truncated.** Each of before/after ran through `truncate_cell` (a 1,500-char *prefix*). When a cell's divergence sat past the cutoff, before and after truncated to the identical prefix and the change vanished.\n\n## The fix\n\n- **Reproduced first** as four failing tests, then fixed.\n- Defect 1: both the markdown brief (`_cell_diff_lines`) and the HTML owner view (`gen_open_items._chain_row`) now collapse the §A5.1 split for a `Drafted` row — it owes a *first* approval wholesale, which its heading already states. Fixing the HTML too keeps the two renderers in agreement (IF-074).\n- Defect 2: a changed cell's before/after renders **whole**; the generous cap stays on the context surfaces (anchor Requirement/Rationale, whole-row bullets). The HTML view already rendered changed cells whole via `word_diff`, so defect 2 was markdown-only.\n- Housekeeping the fix forced: reviewed `trace.py` module-size baseline bump (+8 SLOC), decomposition of `_chain_row` (`_changed_cell_groups`/`_changed_cell_lines`) to stay under the C901 ratchet, and the one-non-literal-LF-site re-pin.\n- The **\"approved, then demoted\" vocabulary gap (decision 9)** is an enum/ladder question orthogonal to these renderer bugs, so it's **banked with a pointer** (decision 9 + the Deliverable) for a trunk sitting to mint as its own OI — a worker branch doesn't mint coordination ids.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Full unfiltered suite: **3225 passed, 9 failed, 24 skipped**. The 9 failures are the pre-existing **ruff-0.16 scaffold-lint skew** (`check_harness`/`dispatch`/`integrate` end-to-end tests failing on `from demo import add` I001 in the generated bootstrap demo) — my diff touches only `trace.py`, `gen_open_items.py`, and four test files, none of those modules or the scaffold generator. Every test in the touched areas passed.\n- Pre-commit check bar green (including `format`).\n\n## Close\n\nDeliverable filled (before Context), `specref` cleared, log fragment written, spec moved via `spec_move.py` to `docs/archive/work/complete/`, final commit carries the `WI: WI-554` trailer. Working tree clean.\n\nOne note: this checkout had no `.venv` — I bootstrapped one (`python3 -m venv .venv` + pip `pytest pytest-xdist pytest-cov ruff`) to run the harness, since the system `python3` had neither pytest nor ruff."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":777,"cache_read_input_tokens":201459,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":777},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7ad1cd60-b0a6-4f35-8617-d6fa089a3cf6","uuid":"657970f1-f938-4ce2-be83-8b79df000e6f","request_id":"req_011CedMy8CWumB4tA9P66jCM"}
